Rikai-Mobile
Copyright 2026 Rikai-Mobile contributors

Rikai-Mobile is an offline Android Japanese reader and dictionary. It adapts
open-source OCR code and loads user-supplied dictionaries. This NOTICE lists
the upstream projects and the changes made for Rikai-Mobile.

Adapted source code
===================

Screen Translator / overlay-translator
--------------------------------------
Copyright 2026 ciddwd
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Source: https://github.com/ciddwd/overlay-translator

Rikai-Mobile adapts the ONNX Runtime OCR pipeline from overlay-translator
(PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5 detection/recognition, manga-ocr recognition, orientation
classification, reading-order sorting, DBNet post-processing). The extraction
is minimal: overlay, capture, translation, ASR, speech, ML Kit, cloud OCR and
bubble-rendering layers are not included. See
third_party/overlay-translator/MODIFICATIONS.md for details. The upstream
LICENSE and NOTICE are retained in third_party/overlay-translator/.

PaddleOCR4Android
-----------------
Copyright 2026 jangviktor-web
Licensed under the MIT License.
Source: https://github.com/jangviktor-web/PaddleOCR4Android

Rikai-Mobile evaluated PaddleOCR4Android's Paddle-Lite/OpenCV library module
and keeps it as a documented optional backend. The MVP does not compile its
native module; horizontal OCR uses the PP-OCRv5 ONNX models instead. The
upstream MIT license is retained in third_party/paddleocr4android/.

